{"title":"Exact sequence","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>An <b>exact sequence</b> is a sequence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a5a7932db3574e02d9945706ec1ca2149c20e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_0 \\stackrel{\\lambda_1}{\\to} A_1 \\stackrel{\\lambda_2}{\\to} A_2 \\stackrel{\\lambda_3}{\\to} \\dotsc \\stackrel{\\lambda_n}{\\to} A_n\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"21\" />\nof <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Homomorphism\" title=\"Homomorphism\">homomorphisms</a> between <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Group_with_operators\" title=\"Group with operators\"> groups with operators</a>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> such that the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Image\" title=\"Image\">image</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f9092807df2606b64909623baacf32bf722daff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kernel\" title=\"Kernel\">kernel</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a10e19efdfb03f5e28ef07be5550bdce13b703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>This notion appears most often when the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Module\" title=\"Module\">modules</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Exact_sequence&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" 